From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:19:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ALSA: hda/acpi: use pm_ptr() for the PM ops

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167235

Wrap hda_acpi_pm in pm_ptr() so that the dev_pm_ops structure and the
suspend/resume callbacks it points to are discarded by the compiler when
CONFIG_PM is disabled, instead of being kept alive by the .pm pointer.
The callbacks are already declared through SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS() and
RUNTIME_PM_OPS(), which only fill the structure under CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
and CONFIG_PM; pm_ptr() completes that pattern and brings the driver in
line with the other HDA controller drivers (intel.c, tegra.c and
cix-ipbloq.c all use pm_ptr()).

No functional change on a CONFIG_PM=y kernel. Follow-up to
commit a41da0bb086e ("ALSA: hda/acpi: add runtime PM suspend/resume to
the ACPI controller"), which is cherry-picked as the previous commit;
this cleanup is not part of that upstream commit and is being sent
upstream separately.

Signed-off-by: David Cemin <dcemin@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9b7453d3cb43fd8d7a2cdf0cc2613fc528977147 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00618
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@3024a5634b2d84f6663ccdf78d913bf805f8b40a
---
 sound/hda/controllers/acpi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/hda/controllers/acpi.c b/sound/hda/controllers/acpi.c
index 04b261dde22e..d6a998ba5251 100644
--- a/sound/hda/controllers/acpi.c
+++ b/sound/hda/controllers/acpi.c
@@ -353,7 +353,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(acpi, hda_acpi_match);
 static struct platform_driver hda_acpi_platform_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = KBUILD_MODNAME,
-		.pm = &hda_acpi_pm,
+		.pm = pm_ptr(&hda_acpi_pm),
 		.acpi_match_table = hda_acpi_match,
 	},
 	.probe = hda_acpi_probe,
